"""
The lines a log file gained since they were last read, for the agent of
Wolly's log system: where each
file was read to is kept in SQLite, so a restart goes on where it stopped.

A file is known by its first line and by its device and inode: the
SHA-256 of the first line and the two numbers are kept with the offset.
When the first line is another, or the file under the name is another
(device and inode), the file was rotated and is read from its start; when
the file is shorter than the offset, it was cut (copytruncate) and is read
from its start too.  Until the first line of a file is complete nothing is
read from it.  A table made before the device and inode were kept gets
the column added; its offsets hold, and each row takes the numbers of its
file at the next read.

Only whole lines are given: what follows the last line end waits for the
next call.  At most mostTailBytes are read in one call.
"""
import Standard.String (
    String
);
import Standard.Database (
    Database,
    Writing,
    DbError
);

module Wolly.LogTail is
    """
    The most bytes one call reads: 1 MiB.
    """
    function mostTailBytes(): Index
        ensures result = 1048576;

    """
    The most bytes of a first line that the fingerprint takes: 4096.  A
    first line that has no end within them counts with its first 4096.
    """
    function mostFirstLine(): Index
        ensures result = 4096;

    """
    Why the new lines could not be read.
    """
    union TailFailure: Free is
        """
        The file is not there, or not a regular file, or cannot be read.
        """
        case Unreadable;
        """
        SQLite refused to read or keep the offset.
        """
        case Storage is
            error: DbError;
    end;

    """
    Makes the table of offsets, if it is not there, and adds the column of
    device and inode to a table made without it.
    No contract: the outcome is the result of I/O.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function prepareTail(db: &![Database[Writing], R]): Option[DbError];

    """
    The whole lines the file at path gained since the last call for it, each
    with its line end, at most mostTailBytes; empty when there are none.
    The offset kept moves past them.
    No contract: the outcome and the length of the lines are the result of
    I/O.
    """
    generic [R: Region, P: Region]
    function readNew(db: &![Database[Writing], R], path: Span[Nat8, P]): Either[TailFailure, String];
end module.
